BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Green Mountain Monteverdi Ensemble Sings Victoria
DTSTART:20261004T160000
DTEND:20261004T173000
DTSTAMP:20261004T155147Z
UID:bb3f712f97c0b4a5de72e62cbb4517@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The Green Mountain Monteverdi Ensemble of Vermont will perform
  the most beautiful works from the greatest Spanish composer of the early 
 17th Century: Tomás Luis de Victoria. The six-voice ensemble will perform
  Victoria's Requiem Mass\, the Officium Defunctorum\, originally published
  in 1605. This work includes the Mass for the Dead and two motets\, Taedet
  animam meam and Versa est in luctum. The second half of the concert consi
 sts of Victoria's best-loved motets for four and six voices including O Ma
 gnum Mysterium\, O vos omnes\, and Quem vidistis pastores. The exquisite h
 armonies of Victoria\, which sometimes take surprising turns\, will transp
 ort the listener to the glories of the High Renaissance. Directed by Steph
 en Falbel.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Cathedral Church of St. Paul\, 2 Cherry Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/green-moun
 tain-monteverdi-ensemble-sings-victoria-21-09-2026-18-53-07
END:VEVENT
