BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Okemo Valley Foliage Train
DTSTART:20261004T090000
DTEND:20261004T173000
DTSTAMP:20261004T155147Z
UID:1342ece8e939dbfb031857a54e04d6@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Step into Vermont’s most enchanting season aboard a vintage 
 foliage train\, where nearly an hour of scenic mountain views\, brilliant 
 color\, and old‑fashioned rail charm create an unforgettable autumn adve
 nture. As Yankee Magazine notes\, “Fall foliage train tours offer a uniq
 ue opportunity to take in the colors of fall\,” and this ride captures t
 hat magic in a way only a historic train can. Before or after your journey
 \, enjoy our Pop‑Up Fall Festival\, filled with local food trucks\, Verm
 ont artisans\, seasonal treats\, and all the cozy autumn traditions Okemo 
 Valley is known for. Crisp air\, handcrafted goods\, warm flavors\, and sm
 all‑town spirit come together to create a perfect October day. It’s th
 e best of Vermont in fall — vintage rail\, mountain scenery\, and a fest
 ive gathering that’s sure to become a lasting memory. NOTE: Seating is f
 irst come first serve - the vintage train cars are best suited to individu
 al seating or for small groups. Group seating together is not guaranteed.
 \n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Blue Lot on Witalec Rd\, 75 Witalec Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/okemo-vall
 ey-foliage-train-24-09-2026-14-41-56
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rappahannock County
DTSTART:20261004T140000
DTEND:20261004T160000
DTSTAMP:20261004T155147Z
UID:3bfbcce24658731c12031c4befcb12@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Our Fall Festival's cornerstone event\, Rappahannock County is
  an operatic tapestry of stories from the American Civil War\, with music 
 by renowned composer Ricky Ian Gordon and a libretto by Pulitzer Prize-win
 ner Mark Campbell. Premiered in 2011 and inspired by diaries\, letters and
  firsthand accounts\, this moving work gives voice to soldiers\, enslaved 
 people\, families\, and civilians whose lives were forever changed by the 
 nation's defining conflict. This moving work premiered in 2011\, inspired 
 by diaries\, letters\, and firsthand accounts\, gives voice to soldiers\, 
 enslaved people\, families\, and civilians whose lives were forever change
 d by the nation's defining conflict. Set in Virginia but resonating far be
 yond its borders\, this opera explores themes of freedom\, loss\, courage
 \, and reconciliation that remain deeply relevant today. With Gordon's lyr
 ical score and Campbell's poignant libretto\, Rappahannock County offers a
 n intimate reflection on the human cost of war and the enduring power of e
 mpathy and hope. Town Hall Theater\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/rappahanno
 ck-county-15-09-2026-13-57-53
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sculpture in the Season: Open Studio & Halloween at Underhill Iron
 works
DTSTART:20261004T100000
DTEND:20261004T170000
DTSTAMP:20261004T155147Z
UID:367ec5aa304b3ce1423826d9645ad8@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Visit Underhill Ironworks for Fall Open Studio and explore the
  work of Vermont sculptor Gerald K. Stoner. Wander through the gallery and
  outdoor sculpture gardens\, where large- and small-scale steel sculptures
  are displayed throughout the landscape. Experience the work against the b
 ackdrop of Vermont’s fall foliage\, as the changing colors bring a new d
 imension to the sculpture and grounds. See new and recent work\, works in 
 progress\, and sculpture for both indoor and outdoor spaces. 🎃 In the s
 pirit of October\, Halloween vignettes will be tucked around the gallery\,
  adding a seasonal twist to the Open Studio weekend. Sculpture is availabl
 e for purchase\, with delivery and installation options near and far. Octo
 ber 3–4\, 2026 10 AM–5 PM both days Underhill Ironworks Underhill\, Ve
 rmont Can’t make Open Studio weekend? The gallery and sculpture grounds 
 are open seven days a week.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Gerald K Stoner Sculpture\, 185 RIVER RD
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/sculpture-
 in-the-season-open-studio-amp-halloween-at-underhill-ironworks-17-08-2026-
 10-59-17
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:‘Sounding Joy’ Benefit Concert
DTSTART:20261004T160000
DTEND:20261004T173000
DTSTAMP:20261004T155147Z
UID:6a071e94d2b736200fc4de3214298c@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Grace Church Choirs and local musicians will offer a concert i
 n aid of Habitat for Humanity of Rutland County Vermont. The concert will 
 include music by Gwyneth Walker\, Saint-Saens\, John Dowland\, Jacob Narve
 rud and Brian Tate performed by Ryan Mangan\, Alexis Scangas\, Josh Bowen
 \, Fred Lemmons\, Heather Masterton Grace Church Sanctuary Choir and the S
 ounding Joy Quartet. The work of Habitat for Humanity depends on the help 
 of the entire community. Consider joining others in contributing your time
  and financial resources to help create safe and affordable housing in Rut
 land. Concert located at 8 Court Street\, Rutland. For more information\, 
 visit gracechurchvt.org Grace Congregational UCC Grace Congregational UCC 
 8 Court Street Rutland \, Vermont 05701 https://gracechurchvt.org/ Submit 
