BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sucka Punch Graffiti Jam
DTSTART:20261004T120000
DTEND:20261004T170000
DTSTAMP:20261004T155147Z
UID:ed0594a14e333e97408beb7a2d9cfa@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Sucka Punch Graffiti Jam is an uplifting celebration of graffi
 ti\, hip-hop culture\, and community — a three-day festival in downtown 
 Brattleboro\, Vermont\, that brings together artists\, youth\, families\, 
 and neighbors. The first and oldest element of hip-hop\, graffiti is a peo
 ple’s art based in storytelling through modern hieroglyphs\, bold letter
 s\, vibrant colors\, and abstract expressions. Sucka Punch brings that ene
 rgy to fall foliage season in Vermont — it’s the festival you didn’t
  see coming! Sucka Punch Graffiti Jam is presented by Juniper Creative Art
 s\, Brattleboro Museum & Art Center\, Downtown Brattleboro Alliance\, and 
 Stone Arch Properties\, with support from The Alchemist Brewery\, Aerosol 
 Legends x NBQ PRO Spraypaint\, Amalgamated Cultureworks\, Homestead Builde
 rs\, Stone Church\, Brattleboro Food Co-Op\, The Void\, the Vermont Arts C
 ouncil\, and the Vermont Community Foundation.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Brattleboro Museum & Art Center\, 10 Vernon Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/sucka-punc
 h-graffiti-jam-21-09-2026-14-32-11
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Many Firsts of Consuelo Northrop Bailey
DTSTART:20261004T140000
DTEND:20261004T160000
DTSTAMP:20261004T155147Z
UID:f4e077632c8fcfbfbdb3052f8d9d00@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Kevin Graffagnino discusses the life and career of Consuelo No
 rthrop Bailey at Pratt Hall. Consuelo was the first woman Lieutenant Gover
 nor of Vermont -- or any state. Born in 1899\, she grew up on her family's
  dairy farm in Fairfield. She attended local schools and graduated from UV
 M in 1921 and then Boston University Law School in 1926. She held a number
  of elected offices including state representative and speaker of the Verm
 ont House of Representatives. She was the first woman to be admitted to pr
 actice before the Vermont Supreme Court. She also represented Vermont on t
 he Republican National Committee from 1936 to 1976. This event is free and
  open to all\, and is sponsored by the Friends of the Montgomery Town Libr
 ary and the Montgomery Historical Society.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Pratt Hall\, 2044 North Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/the-many-f
