BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BAM!: Comics Lab for Kids
DTSTART:20261101T153000
DTEND:20261101T170000
DTSTAMP:20261004T155147Z
UID:4c9c6b92242dfe23485fa456a52ba0@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Comic artist Jon Chad teaches kids to create comics and develo
 p their visual storytelling skills in this six-part series\, with the opti
 on to table at November's Non-Fiction Comic Festival at FFL. Space is limi
 ted\, please register. Ages 8-12. Week 1: What is a Comic? Understanding c
 omics as a storytelling format & building comfort to share ideas. Week 2: 
 Characters & Expression. Create an original main character and strengthen 
 observational & drawing skills. Week 3: Story Beginnings\, Middles & Ends.
  Learn simple story arcs & begin planning a personal comic story\, transla
 ting ideas into structured stories. Week 4: Panels\, Pacing & Speech Bubbl
 es. Experiment with page layouts & how panel size & layout affect storytel
 ling building clarity and communication. Week 5: Guest artist workshop. Ar
 tist shares process\, showing creative careers as attainable & building co
 nfidence through mentorship. Week 6: Finishing\, Sharing & Celebration. Fi
 nalize comics\, completing a self-directed project. Every week through Nov
  01\, 2026.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fletcher Free Library\, 235 College St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/bam-comics
 -lab-for-kids-04-09-2026-22-27-47
END:VEVENT
